# Rosa Kiosk: Professional Design System & Patterns (2025)


## 1. Core Philosophy & Guiding Principles

- **Accessibility First**: All components MUST adhere to WCAG 2.1 AAA contrast ratios (7:1) and follow UC Berkeley's accessible card patterns. Reference: `wcag-contrast-aaa.md`, `ucb-accessible-card-ui.md`.
- **Composition Over Inheritance**: Build complex UIs by composing smaller, single-responsibility components. Reference: `design-principles.md`.
- **Atomic Design Methodology**: Structure components hierarchically as Atoms, Molecules, and Organisms. Cards are considered Organisms. Reference: `atomic-design.md`.

## 2. Component Architecture

### 2.1. Foundation: Radix UI + Tailwind CSS
- **DO** use Radix UI Primitives as the base for all interactive components. This provides accessibility and behavior out-of-the-box. Reference: `radix-primitives.md`.
- **DO** use Tailwind CSS for styling. This aligns with the `shadcn/ui` approach mentioned in other project docs.

### 2.2. Card Components: The Compound Component Pattern
- **DO** build complex components like Cards using the **Compound Component Pattern**. This is the primary pattern for creating flexible and reusable components.
- A Card "organism" should be composed of smaller "atom" or "molecule" components (`Card.Title`, `Card.Body`, `Card.Image`, `Card.Actions`).
- **DON'T** create monolithic Card components with many boolean props (`withImage`, `isDashed`, etc.). This is an anti-pattern.
- **Reference**: The evolution described in `react-component-reusable-scalable-typescript.md` is the canonical guide for this approach.

**Example Card Implementation:**
```jsx
// Card components are grouped
import { Card } from './Card';

// Usage
<Card>
  <Card.Image src="url" alt="description" />
  <Card.Body>
    <Card.Title>My Title</Card.Title>
    <Card.Description>My description.</Card.Description>
  </Card.Body>
  <Card.Actions>
    <Button>Click me</Button>
  </Card.Actions>
</Card>
```

### 2.3. Icon System
- **DO** follow the SVG Icon system pattern outlined in `svg-icons-react-typescript-guide.md`.
- This involves a type-safe `Icon` component that dynamically loads SVGs and allows for runtime color and size props.

## 3. State Management & Data Flow

- **Unidirectional Data Flow**: Data flows down from container components (Handlers) to presentational components (Cards) via props.
- **Custom Hooks**: Encapsulate reusable logic (e.g., data fetching, interaction state) in custom hooks. This is preferred over HOCs. Reference: `hoc-patterns.md` (for understanding the problems they solve).
- **React Context**: Use `Context` only for truly global state like theme, authentication, or session info. Avoid it for passing state that can be passed via props or composition. Reference: `context-api.md`.

## 4. Tavus CVI Integration

> The Tavus CVI library is a core part of the application. Follow these patterns strictly.

- **Provider**: The entire application MUST be wrapped in the `<CVIProvider>`. Reference: `tavus-cvi-overview.md`.
- **Core Components**:
    - Use the `Conversation` block for the main video chat UI.
    - Use the `HairCheck` block for the pre-call device setup screen.
    Reference: `tavus-cvi-blocks.md`.
- **Core Hooks**:
    - Manage call state with `useCVICall` (join/leave).
    - Manage local devices with `useLocalCamera`, `useLocalMicrophone`, `useLocalScreenshare`.
    - Handle permissions with `useRequestPermissions` and `useStartHaircheck`.
    Reference: `tavus-cvi-hooks.md`.

## 5. Accessibility (A11y) Checklist

- [ ] **Contrast**: Text has a 7:1 contrast ratio.
- [ ] **Semantic HTML**: Cards are `<article>` or `<section>`. Titles are `<h2>`/`<h3>`.
- [ ] **Image Alts**: All images have descriptive `alt` text.
- [ ] **Focus Management**: Clear focus indicators on all interactive elements.
- [ ] **Clickable Area**: Interactive elements are large enough (44x44px).
- [ ] **ARIA**: Use `aria-labelledby` and other roles where necessary.

